<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabella II of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1904</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabella II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> became queen as an infant in 1833, and her succession set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlist-wars">Carlist Wars</a>. Her reign was marked by political instability, military coups and scandal at court. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">Glorious Revolution</a> of September 1868 drove her into exile, and in 1874 her son was proclaimed king as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii">Alfonso XII</a>, beginning the Restoration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabella-ii-of-spain.jpg" alt="Isabella II of Spain" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Laurent · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isabel_de_Borb%C3%B3n_y_Borb%C3%B3n-Dos_Sicilias.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
